    "done_when": "A new test, tests/test_verify_gate_replay_is_diagnosable.py, builds a promoted run in a temporary config home whose stored gate command opens with env -C on a worker worktree and names its test file by that worktree's path, removes that worktree, then runs verify-gate at a temporary checkout carrying the same passing test. It asserts the replay ran at the checkout path and reports exit 0, not 125. A second case replays a gate that fails and asserts the result records a log path under the run directory, and that the log holds the failing test id and the replay's stderr. Both cases fail at the base revision (logged) and pass at the head. The negative control, in a scratch copy, restores the discard of the replay's output; the second case fails, with the mutation on the red log's first line and an EXIT= line after pytest's output. The gate is the new test plus the existing test files that call verify_gate; it exits 0, or shows no added failing ids against the base, with both arms recorded as log paths under baseline_suite and after_suite, each ending in an EXIT= line. The tests neither read nor write the real ~/.config/reckon, and assert it untouched.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Plan a-worker-is-charged-to-a-job, followups f-awcj-a-replayed-gate-names-no-worktree, f-awcj-a-replayed-gate-keeps-its-output: a verify-gate replay yields a verdict a reader can act on. Read both followups in docs/plans/a-worker-is-charged-to-a-job.html. The replay near reckon/crew/promotion.py:1095 runs the stored gate command, which can pin a worker worktree the release step has since removed, so the replay exits 125 which is recorded as the gate failing; it also keeps only result.returncode, discarding stdout with stderr. Make the replay rewrite the recorded worker worktree root to the --checkout-path it is replaying at, keeping the replay's own output in a log under the run directory whose path the verify-gate result records. Reuse the log-writing helpers promotion.py already has before adding new ones.",
